  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_whole.rs`: the new function `note_rings_without_floor`. The band that stops at the next flat level calls it before it emits its floor passes.\n- The function reads each outer ring of the band. A ring that stops at the next flat level and has no floor level above it gets one note.\n- The note names the ring and its uncut Z range: `whole-model contour: the ring at (x, y) has no floor level between Z a and Z b - that wall is not cut; reduce the stepdown`.\n- The toolpath moves do not change. Only the notes change.\n- `crates/motion/tests/contour_whole_no_floor.rs`: two new pins.\n- `docs/decisions/2538-contour-ring-no-floor-note.md`: the decision record.\n\n## Cause\n\nA band with two outer rings stops at the next flat level. One ring has a floor level, so the band emits that floor pass. The other ring has no floor level and gets no pass. `forward_band_notes` drops the notes of outer rings when the contour continues. The only other note is given when the whole band emits nothing. Thus the region of the second ring stayed uncut with no note. The first band and the in-between band use the same arm, so the two had the defect.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins, in `crates/motion/tests/contour_whole_no_floor.rs`:\n\n- `first_band_names_the_uncut_range_of_the_ring_without_a_floor_level`: a straight island and a tapered island, each on its plate. The note names Z 3.000 and Z 15.000.\n- `in_between_band_names_the_uncut_range_of_the_ring_without_a_floor_level`: a straight middle step below a boss, and a tapered middle step. The note names Z 5.000 and Z 20.000.\n\nEach pin also asserts that the straight ring keeps its floor pass, and that exactly one ring gets the note.\n\nRed before the fix: yes. Failure text on unchanged code, for the two pins:\n\n```\nassertion `left == right` failed: one ring has no floor level: []\n  left: 0\n right: 1\n```\n\nMutation: `contour_whole.rs` from `upstream/main` put back, the two pins are red. Fix restored, the two pins are green. There is one new guard.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green (motion lib, `contour_whole`, `contour_whole_no_floor`; 4 steps, 0 failed). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc` or `.cl` file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `crates/app/tests/contour_whole_step.rs` was not run. It prints notes in its messages and does not assert them. The fix adds notes only.\n- The first band where no ring has a floor level (for example a part with only a top chamfer) still gives no note. The issue does not include this case. The decision file records it.\n- The pins are not in `crates/motion/tests/contour_whole.rs` as the issue says. That file has 375 lines, and the pins would put it above 400 lines. The new file has the same Gate map.\n- The branch starts from `upstream/main` at `1ae4d061f`. Main moved during the work. The newer commits do not change `contour_whole.rs`.\n- The gate ran without the sccache compile cache. The cache server did not answer compile requests on this machine.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- At the claim, no open PR changed `contour_whole.rs`. This PR is not stacked.\n- #2659 and #2667 (stacked on #2659) opened during this work. They change the same function, `contour_whole_bodies_with`, on different lines. They add `reach_up` and the `cover` lines. This PR adds one call before `forward_band_notes` in the `emitted` branch.\n- A trial merge (`git merge-tree`) of this branch with the head of #2659 and with the head of #2667 is clean.\n- The pins were not run on the merged trees. `reach_up` of #2659 can give more levels to a ring. A ring that gets a level gets no note from this PR, which is correct. Whichever PR merges second refreshes and runs the pins of the two PRs.\n\nChangelog: 2D Contour on a whole model: a ring that has no floor level in a band now gets a note that names its uncut Z range.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2538\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
